.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTFL_SET_THREAD_HOOKS 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_set_thread_hooks
.Nd install libdtfl thread-spawn hooks
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/base.h
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_set_thread_hooks "const dtfl_thread_hooks *hooks"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
By default libdtfl starts worker, network and connection threads with
.Xr pthread_create 3 .
A host that manages its own threads installs thread hooks so that
.Fn dtfl_execute
routes every thread through the host:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef int (*dtfl_thread_fn)(void *(*start)(void *), void *arg,
    void **handle_out, void *ctx);
typedef int (*dtfl_thread_join_fn)(void *handle, void **retval_out,
    void *ctx);
typedef struct dtfl_thread_hooks {
	dtfl_thread_fn spawn;
	dtfl_thread_join_fn join;
	void *ctx;
} dtfl_thread_hooks;
.Ed
.Pp
.Fa spawn
starts
.Fa start Ns Pq Fa arg
on a new thread in the calling process, and stores an opaque handle in
.Fa *handle_out ;
it returns 0 on success or a
.Dv DTFL_E*
code.
.Fa join
waits for the thread named by
.Fa handle ,
stores what
.Fa start
returned in
.Fa *retval_out ,
and returns 0 or a
.Dv DTFL_E*
code.
A handle is joined exactly once.
The
.Fa ctx
member is passed to both.
.Pp
Both
.Fa spawn
and
.Fa join
must be non-NULL.
Passing
.Dv NULL
for
.Fa hooks ,
or a structure with both function pointers
.Dv NULL ,
restores the pthread default.
.Pp
The thread must share the process's memory: the workers of one
.Fn dtfl_execute
exchange data through it.
A PostgreSQL background worker is a separate process, so it cannot back
these hooks.
.Pp
A host that cannot spawn arbitrary threads at all does not install
hooks and does not call
.Fn dtfl_execute .
It drives a single worker on its own thread with
.Fn dtfl_worker_new_standalone
and
.Fn dtfl_worker_step ;
see
.Xr dtfl_embedding 7 .
.Pp
The hooks are process-wide and must be installed before the first
.Fn dtfl_execute ,
like the allocation, panic and log hooks.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or
.Er DTFL_EINVAL
if exactly one of
.Fa spawn
and
.Fa join
is set.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A spawn hook backed by pthreads, the shape a host adapts to its own
thread API:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static int
host_spawn(void *(*start)(void *), void *arg, void **out, void *ctx)
{
	pthread_t *t = malloc(sizeof *t);
	if (pthread_create(t, NULL, start, arg) != 0) {
		free(t);
		return DTFL_EIO;
	}
	*out = t;
	return 0;
}
static int
host_join(void *h, void **ret, void *ctx)
{
	pthread_t *t = h;
	pthread_join(*t, ret);
	free(t);
	return 0;
}

dtfl_thread_hooks hooks = { host_spawn, host_join, NULL };
dtfl_set_thread_hooks(&hooks);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_EINVAL
.It Bq Er DTFL_EINVAL
Exactly one of
.Fa spawn
and
.Fa join
is
.Dv NULL .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_set_alloc_hooks 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_set_log_hook 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7 ,
.Xr dtfl_embedding 7
.Sh HISTORY
Rust's timely dataflow spawns its workers with
.Ql std::thread ;
this hook lets a C host interpose its own thread creation, which an
embedded runtime such as a database server requires.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
.Fn dtfl_set_thread_hooks
must be called before the first
.Fn dtfl_execute .
The
.Fa spawn
and
.Fa join
callbacks run on the thread that starts or joins workers and must be
thread-safe.
